z9x-0009: httpd survives accept()/select() errors from the network; keepalive on connections

Ours (Z9xAirPlay), against FDH2/UxPlay master 3dbf7ce after z9x-0001..0008 (paths relative
to UxPlay/lib). Applied by jni/build_native.sh inside a copy of UxPlay/lib with
patch -p1 --fuzz=0.
- httpd.c: the httpd thread exited for good on any accept() failure or select() error,
  leaving the receiver advertised but deaf. Only EBADF / EINVAL / ENOTSOCK / EFAULT from
  accept() are fatal now; network errors pending on a queued connection, EINTR, EAGAIN
  and EMFILE-class errors (after a 100 ms pause) are retried; EINTR from select() too.
- httpd.c: accepted connections get SO_KEEPALIVE (15 s idle, 3 x 5 s) and
  TCP_USER_TIMEOUT 30 s, so a sender that disappears without closing its connection
  (left Wi-Fi, battery died) is dropped even when it never sends /feedback.
- httpd.c/h, raop.c/h: httpd_is_serving() / raop_is_serving(): 0 once the httpd thread
  has exited (raop_is_running() stays 1 until raop_stop_httpd joins it), so the host can
  notice a dead server and restart it.
